  "notes": "nāma patyate: nāma read as the particle 'indeed'; alternative 'by name'. patyate: denominative 'has mastery, rules'. In line b the object phrase prasthitaṃ somyaṃ madhu stands before the repeated refrain; the English joins it by a colon without adding a verb.",
